  "physical_interpretation": [
    "Native coarse gripper lower-half domain is shown at x1 physical coordinates, x in [0,80] mm and y in [0,40] mm; the gray source solid is a positional guide.",
    "All 3321 node magnitudes are supplied to color scatter in both rows. Exact zero actions are uncolored; nonzero log-color ranges are shared across both rows separately for each component.",
    "Arrows are sampled at logical stride 7, using the 72 saved node indices. Direction arrows are display-scaled shapes with unit shape = 3 display mm; they are not a finite applied displacement.",
    "Material, Hu regularization and total action vectors share one arrow scale: 53.84620886592914 N/mm = 4 display mm. The displayed values are df/dw directional actions with lift held fixed, not force, contact pressure, support reaction or actuator load.",
    "The full three CSC matrices retain all 6642 rows and columns and are not symmetrized. Saved Frobenius asymmetry is material 1.555755192806899e-17, Hu regularization 0.0036932435203595347 and total 1.7130951802337434e-06.",
    "The caption correctly states that multiplying K v by a small parameter step in mm predicts a force increment in N; no step was applied and no equilibrium path was solved.",
    "Forty saved HP evaluations qualify these two declared directions over all local and global entries. This image does not establish exhaustive HP checking of matrix columns, fine-model response, workpiece contact, half-model doubling or executed task targets."
  ],
